<div id="2026-11-13-app-version-and-site-lock" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-13 — Do not hand-bump the app version; site-lock and compare fixes</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The phone update check uses <code>versionCode</code> only, and only when the published code is strictly greater. While this fix was in progress Gemini published APK 48 / 3.4.15 (15:09). That stamp was left as-is. It was not rolled back to 47, and it was not bumped again. The NFS notes no longer show the garbled 3.4.12 text. A checkout <code>version.json</code> with a different code is ignored while the NFS stamp is readable. CSC admin <code>/switch_site</code> is kept across requests. Mobile error logs no longer insert a second <code>system_log</code> row that dropped the username.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Hermes was raising <code>version.json</code> faster than the Android build. A phone will not install a lower <code>versionCode</code>, and a JSON code higher than the APK leaves the update badge stuck. The session-site keep also undid an admin site switch because it required a role row the switch does not.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code>, <code>Root.pm</code>, <code>User.pm</code>, <code>Inventory.pm</code>, <code>root/static/app/version.json</code>, <code>root/admin/schema_compare/fields.tt</code>, <code>tables.tt</code>, <code>root/static/css/themes/schema_compare.css</code>.</p>
</div>
